This patch fixes one of my main pet peeves: Falling through trapdoors
takes you to a random location.

So, now, when you fall through a trapdoor or a hole, you will always end
up in the same randomly chosen location when falling through that
particular trap, except if the level you'll end up on has restrictions
on where you are allowed to land, then the location is random. (The
levels with these exceptions include most of the special levels,
such as Medusa, Wizard's tower, Castle and the Valley.)

This breaks save and bone compatibility.

